########## documented divergence: concurrent owners (N1) ##########
  ok   [append-log] N1 handled by REFUSING a second owner (single-owner lock)
  ok   [sqlite   ] N1 handled by SUPPORTING concurrent owners: A's nonce survives
  ok   [sqlite   ] N1: ...and B's nonce survives an unrelated prune by A
  note: this is the intended difference — the append-log AVOIDS the clobber by
  forbidding a second owner; SQLite makes the clobber impossible, so concurrent
  owners are safe and `single_owner` is accepted-and-ignored.

